      "message": "For the long-term API, where we make surfaces off of any `SkRecorder`, I imagine we will have some form of `makeSurface` on the base `SkRecorder` to make a \"compatible\" surface, whether or not it\u0027s a CPU recorder or a GPU recorder.\n\nGiven that, we do still want a way to explicitly request a CPU surface when a client has a GPU-backed recorder.  I think we need to figure out what that pattern will look like now to make sure we don\u0027t add too much refactoring work later on.\n\nIf a GPU recorder has a `skcpu::Recorder`, this could be: `recorder-\u003e[as|get?]CPURecorder()-\u003emakeSurface()`. But maybe it\u0027s better to leave `makeSurface` for the base class\u0027s functions and have these be `makeCPUSurface` and `makeGPUSurface`.  Or `makeBitmapSurface`, `makeTextureSurface` (I kind of like these because CPU and GPU are easily visually confused).",
